# Logprobs

Log probabilities (logprobs) represent the likelihood of each token occurring in a sequence given the context. A higher log probability signifies greater confidence in the model's output within a specific context.

# API
This PR provides support for logprobs in the experimental [AI Core ](https://sdk.vercel.ai/docs/ai-core)API. Currently, only OpenAI models are supported. I have included logprobs as an OpenAI specific setting, but they could easily be promoted to a general setting. Other providers do support the concept of logprobs, but will be implemented in a separate PR.

All logprobs are unified under the `LanguageModelV1LogProbs` type:
```typescript
export type LanguageModelV1LogProbs = {
  token: string; // the generated token
  logprob: number; // the log probability of this token
  topLogprobs: { // an array of the top `n` tokens that could have been chosen, sorted by log probability
    token: string;
    logprob: number;
  }[];
}[];
```

## OpenAI

|               | generateText | streamText | generateObject | streamObject
| -------- | ------- | -------- | -------- | -------- |
| text        | ✅     |  ✅      | **-** | **-** | 
| json       | **-** |  **-** |  ✅     | ✅     |
| tool       | ❌     |  ❌      |  ❌     | ❌     |

OpenAI supports logprobs on both their `chat` and `completion` APIs, although with slightly different inputs and outputs. This implementation maintains their separate inputs, but unifies their outputs into the `LanguageModelV1LogProbs` type.

### Examples

**Basic Usage**

```typescript
// Generate text with chat
const result = await experimental_generateText({
  model: openai.chat('gpt-3.5-turbo', { logprobs: 3 }),
  system: `You are a helpful, respectful and honest assistant.`,
  messages,
});


// Generate text with completions
const result = await experimental_generateText({
  model: openai.completion('gpt-3.5-turbo-instruct', { logprobs: 3 }),
  system: `You are a helpful, respectful and honest assistant.`,
  messages,
});
```

<details>
<summary>Streaming Text</summary>

```typescript
const result = await experimental_streamText({
  model: openai.chat('gpt-3.5-turbo', { logprobs: 3 }),
  prompt: 'Invent a new holiday and describe its traditions.',
});

for await (const part of result.fullStream) {
  switch (part.type) {
    case 'finish': {
      console.log('Logprobs:', part.logprobs);
      break;
    }
  }
}
```

</details>

<details>
<summary>Generating Object</summary>

```typescript
const result = await experimental_generateObject({
  model: openai.chat('gpt-3.5-turbo', { logprobs: 3 }),
  schema: z.object({ ... }),
  prompt: 'Generate a lasagna recipe.',
  mode: 'json',
});
console.log(result.logprobs);
```
</details>

<details>
<summary>Streaming Object</summary>

```typescript
const result = await experimental_streamObject({
  model: openai.chat('gpt-3.5-turbo', { logprobs: 3 }),
  schema: z.object({ ... }),
  prompt: 'Generate a lasagna recipe.',
  mode: 'json',
});
for await (const part of result.fullStream) {
  switch (part.type) {
    case 'finish': {
      console.log('Logprobs:', part.logprobs);
      break;
    }
  }
}
```
</details>

**Notes**
- Since OpenAI completions do not support generating or streaming objects, nor tools, logprobs are only available when generating or streaming text (when using completions).
- When generating or streaming objects, json mode must be selected as OpenAI does not provide logprobs for tool usage.
- Setting `logprobs` to 0 will return the logprobs for the tokens that were actually provided. Setting `logprobs` to 1 or more will populate the `top_logprobs` array, which is a list of the highest scoring logprobs (up to 20). The first `logprob` in this list will be the one that was chosen, so setting the `logprobs` property to 1 is somewhat pointless. Either set to 0 or 2+.

