[Amazon Bedrock Guardrails](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails.html) can be used to implement safeguards and modify model responses.

This PR alllows for a guardrail config to be passed, and returns trace information (when tracing is enabled) in provider metadata.

## Example

```ts
const result = await generateText({
  bedrock('anthropic.claude-3-sonnet-20240229-v1:0'),
  experimental_providerMetadata: {
    bedrock: {
      guardrailConfig: {
        guardrailIdentifier: '1abcd2ef34gh',
        guardrailVersion: '1',
        trace: 'enabled' as const,
        streamProcessingMode: 'async',
      },
    },
  },
});
```

Using trace information:

```ts
if (result.providerMetadata?.bedrock.trace) {
  // ...
}
```

## Possible improvements

### Guarding only the latest message in a conversation

It's possible to guard specific contents of a message using a `guardContent` field ([as per the docs](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/guardrails-use-converse-api.html#guardrails-use-converse-api-call-message)) rather than applying to the whole conversation. It is not immediately clear to me if this is possible to implement using `experimental_providerMetadata`?

`guardContent` isn't allowed right now due to the CoreMessage schema validation.

Without doing this, if a message in a conversation triggers the guardrail then any subsequent messages in the conversation will continue to result in the guardrail being triggered.

