This implementation enables developers to leverage Google's property ordering feature for more consistent, reliable, and high-quality structured outputs from Gemini models, with an API that scales from simple to complex use cases.

## Background

When using a custom baseURL with the Google Generative AI provider, the file URL validation incorrectly uses the custom endpoint instead of the official Google API endpoint. This causes valid Google file URLs (e.g., https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/files/...) to be rejected when a proxy or custom endpoint is configured.

This leads to the AI SDK attempting to download the file content instead of passing the URL directly to the LLM, which results in errors since these file URLs are typically not accessible externally.

## Summary

Fixed the supportedUrls validation in google-provider.ts to always use the default Google API URL (https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta) for file validation, regardless of the configured baseURL. This ensures that Google file URLs are properly validated even when using a custom endpoint for API requests.

Changes:
 - Introduced `DEFAULT_BASE_URL` constant for the official Google API endpoint
 - Modified supportedUrls regex to use `DEFAULT_BASE_URL` instead of the configured baseURL
 - Added test case to verify file URL validation works correctly with custom baseURL

