## Background

when `experimental_download` encounters a 404 or invalid URL, there's no way to handle it gracefully. you either throw (which aborts the whole request) or return downloaded content you don't have.

Users need to be able to:
1. Remove broken image/file parts from messages
2. Replace them with placeholder text like "[Image unavailable]"
  

## Summary

extended `experimental_download` return types:

```typescript
type DownloadFunctionResult =
  | { data: Uint8Array; mediaType: string | undefined }  // downloaded
  | URL  // passthrough
  | string  // text replacement
  | null;  // remove
  });
```

breaking change to experimental API: null now means "remove" instead of "passthrough", return the URL to passthrough.

```typescript
// Before
if (isUrlSupportedByModel) return null;

// After
if (isUrlSupportedByModel) return url;
if (res.status === 404) return null;
if (res.status === 403) return '[Access denied]';
  });
```

This is a breaking change, but experimental_ APIs, but keeping the old implementaiton made it really. bad.

