## Background

OpenAI added a `phase` parameter with the gpt-5.3-codex launch (Feb 24, 2026). The `phase` field appears on assistant message items in the Responses API and labels a message as either intermediate `commentary` or the `final_answer`. Users who are using codex models may experience early stopping without the phase param being preserved across turns, so performance will be degraded.

## Summary

Add support for the `phase` field (`commentary` | `final_answer`) on assistant message items in the OpenAI Responses API:

- **Schema** (`openai-responses-api.ts`): Added `phase` to `OpenAIResponsesAssistantMessage` input type, response schema, and streaming chunk schemas (both `output_item.added` and `output_item.done`)
- **Provider metadata** (`openai-responses-provider-metadata.ts`): Added `phase` to `ResponsesTextProviderMetadata`, accessible via `providerMetadata.openai.phase`
- **Response parsing** (`openai-responses-language-model.ts`): Reads `phase` from parsed message output and includes it in `providerMetadata` for both non-streaming and streaming paths (`text-start` and `text-end` events)
- **Input conversion** (`convert-to-openai-responses-input.ts`): Reads `phase` from `providerOptions` on assistant text parts and includes it on assistant messages sent back to the API in follow-up requests


